1
00:05:56,250 --> 00:06:02,250
A City Held In The Grip Of Fear. One Man Fearless Enough To Stop It.

2
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:58,500
Open Fire is a action film directed by Kurt Anderson.

3
00:17:48,750 --> 00:17:54,750
Mercenaries leads from Kruger seize an entire city,
and one man sets out to stop them.

4
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:51,000
Alec Mcneil, played by Jeff Wincott.

5
00:29:41,250 --> 00:29:47,250
Lynne Tolbert, played by Mimi Craven.

6
00:35:37,500 --> 00:35:43,500
Kruger, played by Patrick Kilpatrick.

7
00:41:33,750 --> 00:41:39,750
Bob McNeil, played by Lee de Broux.

8
00:47:30,000 --> 00:47:36,000
Special Agent Davis, played by Arthur Taxier.

9
00:53:26,250 --> 00:53:32,250
Walter the Guard, played by Bert Remsen.

10
00:59:22,500 --> 00:59:28,500
Open Fire is single British television crime drama film, made for
ITV, which first broadcast on 12 November 1994.

11
01:05:18,750 --> 01:05:24,750
The film was written and directed by Paul Greengrass, and concerns the police manhunt for David Martin, who escaped from custody
following his arrest for shooting a police officer, leading up to the shooting in error of another man, Stephen Waldorf.

12
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
The film starred Rupert Graves as Martin, as well as Samuel West as Waldorf, Douglas Hodge
as investigating officer DC Peter Finch, and Kate Hardie as Sue Stephens.

13
01:17:11,250 --> 01:17:17,250
Open Fire was filmed in Belsize Park and in around Hampstead, London.

14
01:23:07,500 --> 01:23:13,500
The film has never been released commercially.

15
01:29:03,750 --> 01:29:09,750
The UK based TV Channel Talking Pictures TV has since
shown Open Fire, firstly on 5 October 2024.
